    {
      "title": "CAP Theorem",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CAP Theorem",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Guarantees",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Consistency==: every read sees the latest write",
                "==Availability==: every request gets a non-error response",
                "==Partition tolerance==: keeps working when the network splits"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. CP vs AP",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Partitions are **unavoidable**, so the real choice is ==C or A== during a partition",
                "With no partition you can have {green:both}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CP",
                "AP"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Under partition",
                  "Refuses or errors some requests",
                  "Answers, maybe stale"
                ],
                [
                  "Afterwards",
                  "Stays consistent",
                  "Reconciles later"
                ],
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "HBase, MongoDB (majority writes)",
                  "Cassandra, DynamoDB default"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Not the ACID C",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Two different Cs",
              "text": "CAP 'C' is ==linearizability==. ACID 'C' means constraints hold."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not pick CA?** Partitions happen, so you choose C or A",
                "**Is CAP's C the ACID C?** No: latest-write reads versus constraints"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ACID vs BASE",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ACID vs BASE",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. ACID",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Letter",
                "Guarantee"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==A==tomicity",
                  "all or nothing"
                ],
                [
                  "==C==onsistency",
                  "constraints hold"
                ],
                [
                  "==I==solation",
                  "concurrent transactions do not interfere"
                ],
                [
                  "==D==urability",
                  "committed data survives crashes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. BASE and quorum",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**BASE**: Basically Available, Soft state, ==Eventual consistency==",
                "Replicas {green:converge} if writes stop",
                "A read right after a write may return {red:old data}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "N = replicas holding the data; W = acks needed for a write; R = replicas that answer a read",
                "==R + W > N==: every read set shares a node with the latest write set",
                "N=3, R=2, W=2: 2 + 2 = 4 > 3, so reads see the latest write"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "cards",
              "spec": {
                "cards": [
                  {
                    "title": "Node 1",
                    "lines": [
                      "in W set",
                      "has the write"
                    ],
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Node 2",
                    "lines": [
                      "in W and R",
                      "overlap: latest"
                    ],
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Node 3",
                    "lines": [
                      "in R set",
                      "may be stale"
                    ],
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which to use",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ACID",
                "BASE"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "money, inventory, orders",
                  "feeds, counters, carts, analytics"
                ],
                [
                  "Puts first",
                  "correctness",
                  "availability, scale"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Tunable",
              "text": "Lower R or W for speed; keep ==R + W > N== for fresh reads."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Replication and Sharding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Replication and Sharding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Replicate vs Shard",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Replication",
                "Sharding"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Data",
                  "**Same** data on many nodes",
                  "**Different** data per node"
                ],
                [
                  "Scales",
                  "{green:Availability}, reads",
                  "{blue:Writes}, storage"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Replication Modes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write",
                    "sub": "to leader",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Replicate",
                    "sub": "to followers",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Follower read",
                    "sub": "may be stale",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Leader-follower==: writes go to the leader, followers serve reads",
                "==Replication lag== causes {red:stale reads}",
                "==Multi-leader== and ==leaderless==: several nodes accept writes",
                "Conflicts need resolution: ==last-write-wins==, `vector clocks`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Sharding",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Range",
                "Hash"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Range scans",
                  "{green:Supported}",
                  "{red:Broken}"
                ],
                [
                  "Load",
                  "{red:Hotspots}",
                  "{green:Even}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Consistent hashing==: adding or removing a node moves only about **1/N** of keys",
                "Bad shard key = **hot shard**: low cardinality, or monotonic id"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Shard key",
              "text": "The ==shard key== decides load spread and query cost."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Choosing a Database and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Choosing a Database and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Start from the workload",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Ask first: ==queries==, read/write ratio, consistency need, data size and growth",
                "Default to ==PostgreSQL== unless a clear need rules it out",
                "It also handles {blue:JSON columns}"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Typical fits",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Store",
                "Fits"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Redis",
                  "Cache, sessions"
                ],
                [
                  "MongoDB",
                  "Catalogs, content"
                ],
                [
                  "Cassandra",
                  "Time-series, event logs"
                ],
                [
                  "Neo4j",
                  "Recommendations, fraud rings"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "NoSQL for scale you do not have, then needing ==joins and transactions== later",
                "One database for everything"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Primary store",
                    "sub": "PostgreSQL",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sync",
                    "sub": "copy changes",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cache or search index",
                    "sub": "Redis, search",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Polyglot persistence",
              "text": "One ==primary store== plus a cache or search index **synced from it**."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Default store?** PostgreSQL; JSON columns cover flexible data.",
                "**Why not NoSQL early?** No scale need, then joins and transactions are missing.",
                "**Polyglot persistence?** A primary store plus a synced cache or index."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
